## Summary of behavior

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| No flags, dest write-protected | Error, status 1 |
| `-f`, dest write-protected | Overwrite, status 0 |
| `-i`, dest exists, stdin="y\n" | Prompt on stderr, overwrite, status 0 |
| `-i`, dest exists, stdin="n\n" / " y" / "" / EOF | Prompt on stderr, no change, status 1, continue |
| `-i -f` (last is force) | No prompt, overwrite (even write-protected) |
| `-f -i` (last is interactive) | Prompt, then overwrite or decline |
| `-i`, dest missing | No prompt, move proceeds |
| Identical src/dest | Error regardless of policy |
| Type mismatch (dir↔non-dir) | Error regardless of policy |

**Interpretation chosen:** "Initial ASCII y or Y" means the first byte of the input line (after stripping the trailing newline) must be exactly `0x79` or `0x59`. Any other first byte—including whitespace—causes a decline. The prompt text is written to stderr and flushed before reading stdin.
