        }
        Err(_) => false,
    }
}
```

This uses `BufRead::read_line` (available via the `BufRead` import) to consume one line from stdin, then checks the first character is `y` or `Y`. The `lock()` call returns a `StdinLock` which implements `BufRead`, avoiding any trait-scope ambiguity.

